1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:05,437
We will share a simple engineering
convention across Claude Code and OpenCode

2
00:00:05,437 --> 00:00:08,018
in the approved Google Cloud workspace.

3
00:00:08,198 --> 00:00:12,964
After a change to the validator, the
workflow calls for a focused test and a

4
00:00:12,964 --> 00:00:14,407
short evidence summary.

5
00:00:14,587 --> 00:00:17,543
Choose a convention you can check from the
result.

6
00:00:17,723 --> 00:00:22,192
That gives you a practical way to verify
that the guidance reached the session.

7
00:00:23,673 --> 00:00:28,805
Project instructions carry conventions
that apply to work in the repository.

8
00:00:28,985 --> 00:00:34,226
In this example, the repository contains
the instruction file used by each

9
00:00:34,226 --> 00:00:35,501
configured client.

10
00:00:35,681 --> 00:00:40,545
Some versions and configurations support
shared instructions or imports.

11
00:00:40,725 --> 00:00:44,607
Check the documentation and what your
session actually loads.

12
00:00:44,787 --> 00:00:48,895
Keep the convention short enough that a
teammate can review it easily.

13
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:55,277
A skill gives the agent a reusable
procedure for a particular job.

14
00:00:55,457 --> 00:01:00,434
Write a clear description, so the client
can decide when the procedure is relevant,

15
00:01:00,434 --> 00:01:04,331
and include the steps and output format in
the body of the skill.

16
00:01:04,511 --> 00:01:07,863
This example contains a test evidence
procedure.

17
00:01:08,043 --> 00:01:12,608
Keep supporting templates with the skill
when the selected client supports that

18
00:01:12,608 --> 00:01:13,013
layout.

19
00:01:14,465 --> 00:01:18,704
The same skill can be placed where each
client is configured to discover it.

20
00:01:18,884 --> 00:01:23,887
Confirm the paths and precedence for the
installed versions, especially if the

21
00:01:23,887 --> 00:01:28,248
workspace provides managed policies or
additional skill directories.

22
00:01:28,428 --> 00:01:33,016
If you maintain two files, keep their
contents aligned and review changes

23
00:01:33,016 --> 00:01:33,582
together.

24
00:01:33,762 --> 00:01:38,753
Treat discovery as something to verify,
rather than inferring it from a filename.

25
00:01:40,215 --> 00:01:43,162
Start a fresh authorized session in each
client.

26
00:01:43,342 --> 00:01:48,293
Give both sessions the same recorded test
results and ask for the training pull

27
00:01:48,293 --> 00:01:49,860
request evidence summary.

28
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:55,080
Check that the returned text includes the
command, the outcome, and the files that

29
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:56,002
were inspected.

30
00:01:56,182 --> 00:02:00,342
When the client shows a skill invocation,
capture that signal as well.

31
00:02:00,522 --> 00:02:02,786
Confirm the result against the input.

32
00:02:04,257 --> 00:02:07,883
Run an unrelated request about order
identifiers.

33
00:02:08,063 --> 00:02:13,084
The evidence summary procedure should be
irrelevant here, although the repository's

34
00:02:13,084 --> 00:02:15,081
general guidance may still apply.

35
00:02:15,261 --> 00:02:19,070
Look for evidence in the response and any
invocation record.

36
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:24,783
This pairing of one matching request and
one unrelated request is a small behavior

37
00:02:24,783 --> 00:02:29,573
check you can repeat when the description
or installed version changes.

38
00:02:31,048 --> 00:02:35,784
A repository instruction or skill can
describe what an agent should do.

39
00:02:35,964 --> 00:02:39,486
The host and workspace determine what it
is allowed to do.

40
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:45,328
If a test command requires approval, read
and approve the exact command only in the

41
00:02:45,328 --> 00:02:46,897
authorized environment.

42
00:02:47,077 --> 00:02:51,941
The training reviewer still checks the
final result and records any pull request

43
00:02:51,941 --> 00:02:53,947
decision using their own account.

44
00:02:55,423 --> 00:03:00,588
Review and version the files through the
repository's ordinary human review

45
00:03:00,588 --> 00:03:01,139
process.

46
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:06,119
Include the exact versions and the
outcomes of your matching and unrelated

47
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:07,546
tasks in the evidence.

48
00:03:07,726 --> 00:03:12,452
A teammate should be able to reproduce the
behavior and see why the instructions

49
00:03:12,452 --> 00:03:13,751
belong in the project.

50
00:03:13,931 --> 00:03:18,613
The next lab applies these conventions to
a change across several files.
